// The Vibrant Gio development workspace: all 36 modules of the organization,
// resolving each other from the working tree instead of from published tags.
//
// The members live under .repos/, which is gitignored — this file is committed
// but the checkout it points at is not. Run scripts/clone-all.sh first; without
// it every `use` line below dangles.
//
// Generated by B2.1 from `find .repos -name go.mod`. Regenerate it the same
// way rather than hand-editing: 19 repository roots (workbench has no root
// module), 10 nested modules, and workbench's 7 applications.
//
// The `go` directive matches all 36 members exactly. Do not let it drift up to
// the toolchain's version — the workspace would then build under different
// language semantics than GOWORK=off, which is what CI and every consumer see.
//
// No member may carry a `replace` directive: committed in a public module, it
// breaks every consumer outside this tree. scripts/check-no-workspace.sh
// enforces both halves.

